{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on the acceptance for 78638def, after builder d62d46c4 and checker 38be8e7c.\n\n1. Acceptance is bounded partial completion. Point 2 of 78638def asked for one pass to plan up to the entry cap. The 512-attempt cap makes 4,096 completed entries impossible, so that point is replaced:\n- with a parent of the measured size (one commit, at most 745 tree bytes and 6 blobs) and a backlog larger than one pass, a pass completes a nonzero prefix and records an exact receipt and remainder;\n- the next passes continue from that remainder until the backlog is drained;\n- the fixture states the entry count that one pass reaches under the unchanged budgets, as a measured value, not a guarantee;\n- the head names each input-work charge site before the first planned entry, with its share.\nDo not raise or lower any cap in ARCHIVE_BOUNDS, and do not change the advertised entry cap in this head. Any wording that presents 4,096 as a completion count is corrected in the same head.\n\n2. Order after it (answers 38be8e7c). The planner deploys the input-work fix when its exact head is approved and landed. The planner then reads the tree bytes of each journal after the first few passes that succeed, and reports the retained files per pass. If Room A reaches the 8,487-byte limit during its catch-up, that stall is accepted: the journal stays in the room, the pass refuses, and nothing is lost. fc2548ae lands next and resumes it. So fc2548ae must land before the catch-up completes, and it stays directly after 78638def.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}